She teaches Management and Organizations at New York University Florence and Global Strategy at BIG Academy, an executive education programme for managers and business leaders. She has also held visiting positions at leading international institutions, including New York University Stern School of Business and Warsaw School of Economics.

Sara served as Co-Chair of the EURAM 2025 Annual Conference “Managing with Purpose”, hosted by the University of Florence, and is currently part of the leadership team of EURAM SIG 02 – Corporate Governance, where she serves as Programme Chair-Elect for EURAM 2026.

